WEBVTT

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:05.060
D-Damn you!

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:06.780
Ship in the Sky!

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:12.340
F-False utopia...

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.400
A world without gods...

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.200
cannot be allowed to exist!

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:20.110
We've been chosen.

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:23.420
Not by the gods, and not by destiny.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:26.290
You've chosen me, and I've chosen you!

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:30.130
It must be something 
that can't be achieved alone.

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:32.160
It's meant to be achieved together.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:36.480
Our eternity exists in the 
world that we will change!

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.120
I-Impossible!

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:46.580
Your time is over.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:49.940
We'll create this world with our own hands!

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:56.450
<i>Humans will write their own history...</i>

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:00.980
<i>My work here is... done.</i>

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:12.250
<b>#12 In This Wonderful World</b>

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:25.490
Jeanne d'Arc and the Alchemist Knight

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:47.280
You mere humans want 
to create your own world...

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:49.980
Your own utopia?

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:51.760
I will not allow it!

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:54.110
Absolutely not!

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:00.870
Mur d'Air!

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:07.440
Montmorency, give me elixir!

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:08.520
All right!

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:36.480
I've secured your wrist with Mur d'Air!

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:37.650
Go, Jeanne!

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:08.690
Face your demise!

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:34.960
He wasn't as strong as we feared.

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:37.180
Yep.

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:41.740
It's over.

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:46.040
God bless France!

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:48.040
God bless the saint!

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:49.760
God bless Princess Charlotte!

00:04:55.080 --> 00:05:00.500
King Solomon, Clovis I, Otto the Great,

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:03.260
Jesus Christ, King Arthur...

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:10.160
Maybe you two can achieve what none 
of the other Ulysses that I guided could...

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:14.410
Ulysses Noire?!

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:24.500
It's not over.

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:29.920
Nothing is over yet, Philip.

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:33.610
No. It's over, Father.

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:40.080
If France were to win this battle
and their princess crowned,

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:42.840
England would be in a tough position,

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:47.000
as would Burgundy which assisted them!

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:50.950
You must eliminate the root 
of trouble while you can!

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.660
Kill the white Ulysses.

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:54.740
I can't!

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:56.800
She's Montmorency's...

00:05:56.800 --> 00:05:59.320
Kill them, my daughter!

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:00.830
No!

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:07.020
You will never be with Montmorency.

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:09.300
But that girl...

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:17.350
I can't let that happen.

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:21.440
No... Don't...

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:42.130
Shoot me!

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:44.460
Please!

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:47.130
Put an end to my living hell!

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:49.040
Please!

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:07.340
Glasdale...

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:10.150
You missed again?

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:15.160
No, it was right on target.

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:19.780
I finally completed a worthwhile mission.

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:22.480
Did you see that?

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:44.380
Ulysses, and gods...

00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:47.020
What's happening with this battle?

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:51.680
Lord Talbot!

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:56.040
You want us to retreat?!

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:59.450
Yes, that's the order from Lord Bedford.

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:02.880
The Tourelles complex has indeed fallen.

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:05.840
However, the French army must be in tatters.

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:07.080
We can still fight!

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:09.280
Yes, of course!

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:13.240
I have no doubt in my mind that 
our hero, Lord Talbot, would be victorious...

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:16.090
...if this were an ordinary battlefield.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:19.850
Our enemy's morale is at an abnormal level.

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:22.240
They're all fighting like martyrs.

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:25.350
It would be very taxing to fight them.

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:27.840
B-But if we were to retreat,

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:32.720
the story of maiden Jeanne's reputation 
and glory will become a legend.

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:37.780
Perhaps, it will become a part 
of French history for all eternity.

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:40.500
This is what Lord Bedford 
has to say about that...

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:42.120
"It won't be that way."

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:45.520
It means he has an amazing strategy

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:48.640
to prevent that from happening 
to the white Ulysses!

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:58.180
And you are the important fighting 
capability we need to make that happen!

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:00.720
We can't risk losing such an important asset.

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:03.680
Don't be ashamed and retreat!

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:04.520
Yep!

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:09.420
Very well. I will trust Lord Bedford.

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:10.770
Okay!

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:19.900
We have confirmed the 
retreat of the English army.

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:24.790
Looks like it's over... for now.

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:53.220
Orléans will not forget about 
this miracle until the end of time!

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:54.840
For all eternity!

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:57.570
Let's celebrate, and designate 
today as a day of thanksgiving!

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:02.720
Please make me your wife!

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:04.680
I wouldn't mind just being a concubine!

00:10:04.680 --> 00:10:07.580
Please spend a night with us!

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:09.960
Batard-sama!

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:12.680
Stay away!

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:17.720
My heart already belongs to Alençon!

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:20.660
Oh, is that why you're cross-dressing?

00:10:20.660 --> 00:10:22.970
That's love! That's true love!

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:25.000
Ladies, that's a misunderstanding!

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:26.600
Just think of it as saving me!

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:32.240
I can't believe this!

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:35.420
Mercenaries like us were nuisances 
no matter where we went,

00:10:35.420 --> 00:10:38.240
but now the girls are all over us!

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:40.860
Well, good for you.

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:43.370
Make sure to do your business 
while you're still popular.

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:45.160
Whoa! Hold on there!

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:48.660
You'll always be the one
 I care about the most.

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:52.180
I'll forget about the baiser 
with that punk Montmorency.

00:10:52.180 --> 00:10:54.740
Come on! Spend the night with me today.

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:57.700
Aren't you eating too much?

00:10:57.700 --> 00:11:00.900
I've been getting abnormally hungry 
ever since I became Ulysses.

00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:05.480
Excess fat usually goes 
to my breast, but there's a limit.

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:08.140
This must be a side effect of Joyeuse.

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:10.660
Damn you, Montmorency! 
Where have you run off to?

00:11:10.660 --> 00:11:11.780
Explain what's happening to me!

00:11:11.780 --> 00:11:15.400
Are you trying to turn me into a pig?!

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:20.060
I didn't have any other choice!

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:24.620
The Philosopher's Stone would've killed 
La Hire if I didn't baiser her then.

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:29.120
It was simply a replenishment 
of elixir, and nothing more!

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:30.700
Do you understand?

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:33.100
I understand.

00:11:34.740 --> 00:11:37.920
You want La Hire to be your second wife!

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:40.700
No! That was never what I intended,

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:43.440
and Catherine only became 
my wife as a formality!

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:46.050
I explained it to you countless times!

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:52.560
Is that how a saint should behave?

00:11:56.020 --> 00:11:57.920
Jeanne!

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:02.340
I thought we'd never meet again!

00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:07.320
I'll never leave you again.

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:11.100
You're hugging me too tightly! 
I can't breathe!

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:18.860
You can just kiss me on my cheeks! 
This is embarrassing!

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:23.520
Then let me kiss your belly.

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:27.320
Oh, my! Such a cute belly!

00:12:27.320 --> 00:12:30.460
You're tickling me, Charlotte!

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:32.440
Not my belly!

00:12:32.440 --> 00:12:35.850
We can't let the nobles see this.

00:12:39.720 --> 00:12:45.360
La Hire, we can't thank you enough 
for saving Jeanne and Montmorency.

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:49.740
Tsk, I would've preferred land over a medal.

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:51.370
Montmorency.

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:52.420
Yeah.

00:12:52.420 --> 00:12:56.630
I will give you the title of 
General of the French Army.

00:12:56.630 --> 00:12:58.400
Huh? Me?!

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:01.180
I'm happy with just being an alchemist.

00:13:01.180 --> 00:13:02.760
No, that's not good enough.

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:05.620
To have a truth or continue fighting...

00:13:05.620 --> 00:13:10.040
The nobles in the palace 
have yet to be united.

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:13.020
I'm certain they'll try to conspire
 against Jeanne again.

00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:15.360
It's for you to protect Jeanne.

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:18.040
Montmorency, starting today,

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:20.700
you are the highest ranking 
commander of the French army.

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:22.080
General Gilles de Rais.

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:26.700
Fine, but on one condition.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:29.620
Try your best to make up with Richemont.

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:35.960
I-I know! I've already practiced 
begging for forgiveness!

00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:52.540
What are you doing?

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:58.100
Are you going to leave without telling us?

00:13:58.100 --> 00:14:01.200
I-I don't need your permission to leave.

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:05.280
How can the Guardian of the Philosopher's Stones
 just abandon the stones?

00:14:06.340 --> 00:14:08.360
I'm no longer fit to be a guardian.

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:12.180
I couldn't even predict 
the opening of Babylon's Hole.

00:14:13.020 --> 00:14:15.920
I almost let you and Jeanne die.

00:14:15.920 --> 00:14:18.200
I was totally helpless.

00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:21.660
You opened up the path 
to the future on your own.

00:14:22.860 --> 00:14:25.000
My usefulness has ended.

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:27.480
Now, I'm useless.

00:14:27.900 --> 00:14:30.860
What's the deal? This isn't like you.

00:14:30.860 --> 00:14:34.200
"Useless" is the word 
for insulting me, right?

00:14:34.970 --> 00:14:38.160
Don't you think my existence is creepy?!

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:39.980
Are you stupid or something?

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:44.540
I audaciously ordered you to create 
a utopia on our first encounter,

00:14:44.540 --> 00:14:47.680
and I knew about the existence 
of Babylon's Hole and Enlil...

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:49.900
Why aren't you suspect of my true identity?

00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:51.880
You fool! Moron!

00:14:53.380 --> 00:14:54.980
Hey, Astaroth.

00:14:54.980 --> 00:14:57.420
No matter how much you master alchemy,

00:14:57.420 --> 00:15:00.800
time cannot be regained once it has passed.

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:03.560
In the end, the past is nothing but an illusion.

00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:08.420
The present is the only time 
in which we can live.

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:10.900
Montmorency...

00:15:12.560 --> 00:15:16.840
I stopped your time 
when you were still a child.

00:15:16.840 --> 00:15:21.700
But Jeanne must have moved 
the clock's needle forward.

00:15:23.540 --> 00:15:24.840
If...

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:28.940
If you'll allow me to...

00:15:28.940 --> 00:15:34.220
I want to stay and see you 
and Jeanne write history.

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:37.120
Sure. Please watch over us,

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:38.740
from the VIP seat.

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:46.160
By the way, what was that illusion 
of the beautiful girl all about?

00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:47.600
She's...

00:15:47.600 --> 00:15:52.220
Venus, the goddess of love and war,
is always right beside you.

00:15:53.200 --> 00:15:55.540
What is she to you, anyway?

00:15:55.540 --> 00:15:57.440
Oh, maybe she's your sister?

00:15:57.440 --> 00:15:59.000
You're such a...

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:02.810
<b>Paris</b>

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:07.880
The seventy-two demons 
from an alternate world.

00:16:07.880 --> 00:16:12.860
I wonder if it is related to the legend 
of the famous King Solomon.

00:16:13.440 --> 00:16:14.740
No matter.

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:16.830
They have been vanquished, right?

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:19.240
Who knows?

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:21.450
Gods are not my expertise.

00:16:21.860 --> 00:16:26.140
One other matter, about your partner...

00:16:26.140 --> 00:16:30.620
Is it true that she fell into the 
Loire River and is missing in action?

00:16:30.620 --> 00:16:31.840
Yes.

00:16:37.440 --> 00:16:39.160
You're hard to read, aren't you?

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:41.180
You'll have another mission soon.

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:43.060
Sharpen your arrows and wait for my orders.

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:44.850
Yes, sir.

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:54.980
It should've been destroyed.

00:16:54.980 --> 00:17:00.800
It is not possible to destroy this helm, 
which bears the power of Holy Grail.{timing check please}

00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:07.290
In other words, you cannot escape your fate.

00:17:07.660 --> 00:17:11.880
Now, Philip, take the helm.

00:17:15.380 --> 00:17:17.050
I refuse.

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:20.180
W-Wait.

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:22.360
Come back, Philip!

00:17:22.360 --> 00:17:25.960
You have already sinned as Ulysses Noire. 
There's nowhere left for you to go.

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:28.980
Oh, I see.

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:32.920
You think Montmorency will forgive you?

00:17:32.920 --> 00:17:34.940
Of course.

00:17:34.940 --> 00:17:39.700
I'm sure he would be able 
to gently take my tainted hands.

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:43.580
But you know, Montmorency belongs to Jeanne.

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:46.240
He will never be yours.

00:17:46.840 --> 00:17:50.560
You'll never be able to watch 
over them by their side.

00:17:50.560 --> 00:17:52.090
Right?

00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:01.660
<i>Even so...</i>

00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:06.540
<i>I'll fight my weakness!</i>

00:18:12.740 --> 00:18:14.980
It was a big surprise.

00:18:14.980 --> 00:18:16.920
It was a surprise for me, too.

00:18:16.920 --> 00:18:20.600
I was a heretic, and now I'm suddenly 
the general of the French army.

00:18:20.600 --> 00:18:22.540
It's just absurd.

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:24.040
I'm not talking about that.

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:26.200
It's the fact that you brought her here.

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:31.120
Oh, she insisted on meeting you.

00:18:46.200 --> 00:18:49.500
Jeanne, my marriage to my cousin

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:51.900
is only to pass control 
of this family's...

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:53.100
Please...

00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:57.740
If Montmorency is crying alone...

00:18:58.660 --> 00:19:00.280
When that happens...

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:04.780
please be the one to cheer him up, Catherine.

00:19:12.180 --> 00:19:13.540
<i>I had a dream.</i>

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:21.500
<i>The sky was blue, and 
there was a gentle breeze.</i>

00:19:22.100 --> 00:19:24.080
<i>The sounds of military horses trotting,</i>

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:26.660
<i>and of swords clashing 
were nowhere to be heard.</i>

00:19:27.740 --> 00:19:29.940
<i>The war must be over.</i>

00:19:30.690 --> 00:19:35.060
<i>When I listened in, I heard 
the sound of someone laughing.</i>

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:38.660
<i>In the dream, I knew...</i>

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:45.370
<i>"However, Jeanne is no longer 
in this wonderful world."</i>

00:19:54.260 --> 00:19:55.880
Having a hard time sleeping?

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:57.080
No.

00:19:58.100 --> 00:19:59.560
Did you have a bad dream?

00:20:13.600 --> 00:20:16.110
Come on. Let's go, Jeanne.

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:22.020
Yeah!

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:28.880
Orléans was liberated, and the English 
army retreated a great distance.

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:33.620
General, please announce our next strategy.

00:20:38.620 --> 00:20:42.760
We will cross the Loire River, 
and advance towards Reims!

00:20:42.760 --> 00:20:47.350
We'll crown our princess, 
and make her the true queen of France!

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:49.780
Yeah!

00:20:49.780 --> 00:20:51.800
Allow me to help!

00:20:57.110 --> 00:20:58.320
Sister!

00:20:58.320 --> 00:20:59.610
Lady Richemont!

00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:01.610
Richemont...

00:21:03.020 --> 00:21:05.080
Will you allow me to tag along?

00:21:05.080 --> 00:21:06.160
She can, right?

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:08.370
Of course she can, right? Right?

00:21:09.380 --> 00:21:12.000
That's a very good offer, but...

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:12.800
Huh?

00:21:12.800 --> 00:21:16.370
This isn't a question 
that a general can answer.

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:19.840
So what do you say, Your Majesty?

00:21:22.820 --> 00:21:26.180
I already gave the title 
of general to Montmorency!

00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:28.890
If you're fine with that, 
then you can come with us.

00:21:29.580 --> 00:21:31.520
I'm honored by your words.

00:21:35.220 --> 00:21:38.920
You've become a real knight, Montmorency.

00:21:38.920 --> 00:21:40.900
I hope so.

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:44.400
Take me to the Cathedral de Notre-Dame!

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:47.660
As you wish, Princess.

00:21:49.760 --> 00:21:51.840
Head out!

00:21:56.200 --> 00:21:57.980
Hey, Montmorency.

00:21:57.980 --> 00:21:58.920
Hmm?

00:21:58.920 --> 00:22:00.780
Wanna make a baby?

00:22:02.140 --> 00:22:03.760
Let's do it!

00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:05.550
Let's make one tonight!

00:22:06.020 --> 00:22:08.260
Montmorency! How could you?

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:09.640
Why are you mad at me?!

00:22:09.640 --> 00:22:13.340
Jeanne, please don't say things 
like that with a smile!

00:22:13.340 --> 00:22:14.560
We can't make one!

00:22:14.560 --> 00:22:18.120
What? We can't? Even with a baiser?

00:22:18.120 --> 00:22:22.460
You'd already have lots of children
 if a baiser could give you a baby.

00:22:23.700 --> 00:22:26.740
